  "rationale": "Re-review reason: depends_on declared (DI-36 -> DI-28, DI-20); DI-36 text and test unchanged. Upstream context: DI-20 is the recorder that must write the fingerprints (exercised through the real record_verdict / carry_forward_verdict); DI-28 makes fingerprints scope-dependent (module default) -- new probe: record_verdict fingerprinting at SCOPE_FUNCTION regardless of hash_scope KILLED. Also checked against DI-35 (pins cover upstream text), which DI-36 does not declare but which decides what a stale verdict's 'requirement-text change' is. All 20 recorded probes re-executed one at a time via rdm story mutation-probe; results identical to the prior review (19 KILLED, 1 SURVIVED documented equivalent), plus 2 new probes. Clauses: (1) new verdicts record normalized fingerprints -- empty text_fingerprint KILLED; recorder fingerprinting at the wrong scope KILLED (new); (2) text ignores whitespace -- raw normalize_text KILLED; (3) test source ignores whitespace/comments/docstrings: Python -- skipping _strip_docstrings KILLED; non-Python -- removing the line-comment filter, dropping '//', disabling leading /* */ blocks, never closing a block, keeping block-interior lines KILLED; ONLY comments -- widening '#' to any '#'-leading line, dropping code after '*/' (one-line and multi-line closers), old fail-open '*'-leading regex all KILLED; `after = line` instead of the text after '/*' SURVIVED (equivalent unless a line opens with the degenerate '/*/'); (4) classify A/B/C/D -- swapping C/B precedence KILLED, disabling D KILLED; (4b) a stale verdict caused by an UPSTREAM (depends_on) requirement-text change classifies as C -- NOT COVERED: current_fingerprints fingerprinting the input's own text instead of pinned_text(di, by_id) SURVIVED, because no fixture input declares depends_on; under that mutant every verdict re-opened by an upstream reword (exactly the ten re-opened by this dogfood commit) would classify as A and `rdm story verdict --carry-forward` would re-pin it with no review; (5) class shown in the report -- suppressing the suffix KILLED; (6)-(7) carry-forward re-pins class A and records class/from_hash -- carried_forward=None KILLED; (8) refuses every other class -- admitting B, C, D each KILLED. Verdict partial on (4b). Fix: add a dependent input to the fixture, reword its upstream, and assert class C and a refused carry-forward (and consider declaring DI-36 depends_on DI-35 in the record).",
